# K0 / B002 — Run 2 replica annotation (blind). hook.cjs: single hook dispatcher.

C R3 OL DEP-003,DEP-004,DEP-005 | MUST (PreToolUse: permissionDecision deny; fails closed) | Dependency addition/update commands (npm/pnpm/yarn install|add naming a package, update/upgrade/dedupe, npm audit fix, ng add, ng update <pkg>, dotnet add package, dotnet package add|update, nuget install|update, Install-Package/Update-Package, and restores carrying a force flag) are denied until the add-dependency workflow has been completed; the command is then re-run with the trailing comment `# add-dependency: reviewed`. | Bash/PowerShell commands incl. bash -c / cmd /c / pwsh -Command wrappers | The marker comment is self-certified by the agent; bare restores from the lockfile (npm ci, yarn) pass.
C X1 EX DEP-001,DEP-003 | MUST (PreToolUse deny; PostToolUse confirmation message on removed manifests) | Dependency-removal commands (npm uninstall|remove|rm|r|un|unlink, pnpm/yarn remove, dotnet remove package, dotnet package remove, Uninstall-Package) are likewise denied until the add-dependency workflow has been completed and the command carries `# add-dependency: reviewed`; a removed package manifest is reported for confirmation that the removal was intended and approved. | Bash/PowerShell commands; package manifests | Marker comment after review. | The oracle's dependency policies (DEP-001..DEP-005) govern additions and updates; no oracle policy subjects dependency removal to a review workflow or approval confirmation. | `npm uninstall lodash` is denied until the add-dependency removal checklist was run and the marker is added.
C R4 OL DEP-025 | MUST NOT (PreToolUse deny message) | A dependency command using --force or --legacy-peer-deps (npm -f included) receives the instruction to resolve the actual peer-dependency conflict instead. | npm/pnpm/yarn/ng dependency commands | The force message is attached only while the review marker is absent; with `# add-dependency: reviewed` a forced command is not denied by the hook.
C X2 EX ARC-001,ARC-020,ARC-028,GOV-017 | MUST (Reserved; PreToolUse deny; PostToolUse finding) | Changing the project reference graph (dotnet add|remove reference, dotnet reference add|remove, or a .csproj ProjectReference change) is Reserved unless an accepted decision already requires the reference, even when the new reference would be legal: commands are denied unless they carry `# project-references: approved` after the Decision Request; post-change findings ask to confirm the change was approved and recorded, or revert it. | .NET project references | Reference already required by an accepted decision; marker comment after approval. | ARC-001 already permits inward references and ARC-020 gates consequential changes such as new projects/layers; no oracle policy makes every legal reference edge a Reserved decision. | Adding the standard Api -> Application reference is denied until a Decision Request is approved and the marker is added.
C R5 OL GOV-015 | MUST NOT (PreToolUse: permissionDecision ask) | Repository-changing Git commands (every subcommand not in the read-only list or read-only argument forms, e.g. commit, push, merge, rebase, reset, add, fetch, pull, checkout <target>, stash push, branch/tag changes, config writes) trigger a permission prompt stating they may run only when the user explicitly requested them; procedure git-workflow. | Bash/PowerShell git commands | Read-only forms (status, diff, log, branch --list, stash list, ...) pass.
C X3 EX - | MUST (PostToolUse feedback, decision block) | When instruction files change (CLAUDE.md, the decision register, .claude/** except .hook-state and settings.local.json), check-instructions runs and its errors are fed back to the agent. | Edits/shell commands touching instruction files | Only errors are fed back. | Structural self-validation of the instruction system; not derived from any V2 policy. | Breaking an instruction header or reference is reported immediately after the edit.
